  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 74\u2011year\u2011old woman with a long history of type 2 diabetes diagnosed in 1995, complicated by progressive diabetic nephropathy. Over the past decade her chronic kidney disease has advanced from stage 1 to stage 4, and she is currently awaiting kidney transplantation. She suffered an acute ST\u2011segment elevation myocardial infarction in 2010 and has a prior history of myocardial infarction, coronary artery disease, and aortic valve stenosis treated with valve replacement in 2005. Metabolic syndrome, hypertriglyceridemia, and diabetic neuropathy are present. Socially she reports ongoing stress, intimate\u2011partner abuse, low educational attainment, a criminal record, and is not in the labor force, all of which may affect adherence and follow\u2011up. Current therapy is limited to insulin and low\u2011dose aspirin, with no documented antihypertensives, statins, or renin\u2011angiotensin system blockers.",
